<title>USA: Cirrus Logic completes wireless unit's sale.</title>
<headline>Cirrus Logic completes wireless unit's sale.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cirrus Logic Inc on Friday said it had sold the wireless semiconductor products group of PCSI, its wholly owned subsidiary based in San Diego, California, to Rockwell International Corp.</p>
<p>Net proceeds to Cirrus Logic are $18.1 million in cash, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Last spring we described our intention to streamline operations, to narrow our focus to our long-standing core competencies,&quot; Thomas Kelly, chief financial officer, said in a statement. &quot;This divestiture marks another milestone of progress along that path.&quot;</p>
</text>
